      "rationale": "Allowed types build|chore|ci|docs|feat|fix|perf|refactor|revert|style|test, scope optional, subject must start lowercase; enforced on both the PR title and every commit in the branch range."
    },
    {
      "id": "_sops_creation_rules",
      "label": ".sops.yaml creation_rules (PGP recipients)",
      "file_type": "code",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/.sops.yaml",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Two rules: whole-file encryption for env/sops.*/dockerconfigjson/s3.conf suffixes, and field-level encrypted_regex for plain *.yaml covering ca_password, provisioner_password, root/intermediate CA material, .dockerconfigjson and sql.php. Adding a member means adding a fingerprint and re-running sops updatekeys per file."
    },
    {
      "id": "_vscode_extensions_signageos_vscode_sops",
      "label": "Recommended extension signageos.signageos-vscode-sops",
      "file_type": "code",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/.vscode/extensions.json",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_vscode_settings_sops_enable",
      "label": "VS Code SOPS auto-decrypt settings",
      "file_type": "code",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/.vscode/settings.json",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Files matching a path_regex in .sops.yaml decrypt on open and re-encrypt on save. .conf files have no recognized format so SOPS falls back to the binary store (JSON wrapper with a data key) — which is how s3.sops.conf and the *-ingress-auth.sops.conf files are stored."
    },
    {
      "id": "claude_flux_layer_graph",
      "label": "Flux layer dependency graph (feather-core)",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/CLAUDE.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Root GitRepository -> root Kustomization at ./clusters/feather-core fans out into layers ordered by dependsOn; most use wait:true so a dependent blocks until its dependency is Ready at the same git revision. Forcing reconcile mid-flight creates the churn it tries to clear."
    },
    {
      "id": "claude_two_tier_kustomize_pattern",
      "label": "Two-tier base + cluster overlay Kustomize pattern",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/CLAUDE.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Portable definitions live under infrastructure/base and apps/base; cluster overlays reference a base, patch it, and attach secrets. Overlays set disableNameSuffixHash:true so generated names are stable — the trade-off is that changing a secret does not roll the consuming Deployment."
    },
    {
      "id": "claude_path_spelling_gotcha",
      "label": "feather-core vs feathre-core path spelling gotcha",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/CLAUDE.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "infrastructure uses clusters/feather-core while apps uses the misspelled clusters/feathre-core; both are real, live paths and must not be normalized to each other."
    },
    {
      "id": "claude_sops_workflow",
      "label": "SOPS (PGP) secrets workflow",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/CLAUDE.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Secrets reach pods via Kustomize secretGenerator or generators in an overlay's kustomization.yaml and Flux decrypts at apply time; this worktree's copy claims recipients live in two .sops.yaml files that must stay in sync."
    },
    {
      "id": "claude_ci_conventions",
      "label": "CI and dependency-update conventions",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/CLAUDE.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Conventional Commits enforced by pr-lint, validate.sh run by flux-validate on every relevant PR/push, and Renovate constantly moving main so branches must be rebased before pushing."
    },
    {
      "id": "claude_helm_chart_version_bump",
      "label": "In-repo Helm chart version bump requirement",
      "file_type": "document",
      "source_file": ".claude/worktrees/agent-a5f46601e4bdeb874/CLAUDE.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Flux/Helm caches by chart version, so editing a chart under helm/ without bumping Chart.yaml version leaves the cluster rendering the cached template."
    },
